-- An over-budget `of` enumeration (21845 values, over the 10000 of
-- `defaultMaterializationCardinality`) whose body builds a tuple. The
-- materialization budget gate (tasks of-annotation-forces-dense-enumeration and
-- enumeration-budget-gate-misses-nested-application) declines dense
-- enumeration here and hands the binding to the plan-guided path, whose
-- traversal has no case for a tuple constructor, so the whole compile is
-- refused by the set-witness fallback's diagnostic. Before the gate this
-- compiled densely (a 5,971,459-byte Python module). Dense fallback was
-- explicitly rejected (the user's 2026-09-16 decision on
-- of-annotation-forces-dense-enumeration), so the fix is plan-traversal
-- coverage of the tuple, not re-opening dense enumeration. Nested spellings
-- (`let c = .. in let scene = .. in (numRed scene, c)`, or `numRed scene +
-- (if c then 1.0 else 0.0)`, refused on `InjF plus`) fail the same way.
-- Generate-only compiles (`--noProbability --noIntegrate`) still succeed.
data Color = Red | Green | Blue
data Object = NoObj | Obj color::Color
data Scene = Empty | SCons obj::Object, rest::Scene depth 7

neural readScene :: (Symbol -> Scene) of 7x.{Empty | SCons {NoObj | Obj {Red|Green|Blue}} x}

numRed s = if isEmpty s then 0.0 else (if isObj (obj s) then (if isRed (color (obj s)) then 1.0 else 0.0) else 0.0) + numRed (rest s)

main sym = let scene = readScene sym in (numRed scene, numRed scene)
